SUMMARY:LFS Monthly Discussion - El Serrano's
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\nCome joins us for intelligent d
 iscussion and freethinking fun at our monthly meeting. Lancaster Freethoug
 ht Society is a community for Freethinkers\, Atheists\, Agnostics\, Humani
 sts\, Non-believers\, Skeptics\, and those who are simply curious. There i
 s no fee to attend our meetings which range from topical subjects of inter
 est to freethinkers such as Church/State Separation\, as well as subjects 
 such as science\, philosophy\, ethics\, counter-apologetics\, and psycholo
 gy. All are welcome to attend no matter what your beliefs may be but prose
 lytizing is not allowed. Bring your articles\, news\, jokes\, gripes\, que
 stions\, ideas\, topics\, or anything else you would like to discuss with 
 the rest of the group.\n\nHope to see you there!
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 315057088/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260601T171710Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260601T171710Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Lancaster Freethought Society
UID:event_315468654@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260701T043322Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260704T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260704T173000
SUMMARY:Saturday Freethought Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\n**July 4 Discussion: What Does 
 Real Freedom of Thought Look Like?**\nFreedom of thought is not just the r
 ight to have an opinion. It is the practice of examining what we believe\,
  why we believe it\, and what we do when evidence challenges us.\n\n**Grou
 nd rules**\nWe’ll use timed rounds: up to 2 minutes each\, with the opti
 on to pass. No interruptions. After every 2 rounds\, we’ll open the floo
 r for discussion.\n**Round 1 — Personal Starting Point**\nWhat belief\, 
 assumption\, or habit of thought have you questioned more deeply over time
 ?\n**Round 2 — Pressure**\nWhere do you feel pressure to think\, speak\,
  or stay silent in a certain way?\n**Round 3 — Belief vs. Inquiry**\nCan
  a person be a freethinker and still hold spiritual\, intuitive\, or unexp
 lained beliefs?\n**Round 4 — Responsibility**\nDoes freedom of thought r
 equire evidence\, humility\, or willingness to change your mind?\n**Closin
 g question**\nWhat is one habit of mind you want to practice more delibera
 tely: curiosity\, humility\, courage\, patience\, or willingness to revise
  your view?\n**Come curious. Come ready to listen.**\n\nBecause this is de
 signed as a shared discussion\, we’ll go forward if at least one additio
 nal member beyond the 3 organizers **RSVPs by Friday July 3rd at noon**. O
 therwise\, we’ll reschedule.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/lancaster-freethought-society/events/
 315468654/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260629T133513Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260629T133513Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
